## Original Content
A Chinese team, All Gamers, on Sunday beat double-champions Team Falcons from Saudi Arabia to win the video-gaming Esports World Cup (EWC) held Sunday in Paris.

## Summary
A Chinese esports team, All Gamers, won the Esports World Cup in Paris by defeating Team Falcons from Saudi Arabia on Sunday. The victory is notable as Team Falcons were previous double-champions in the competition.

## Key Points
- All Gamers won the Esports World Cup in Paris.
- Team Falcons, who were double-champions, lost to All Gamers.
- The event was a video-gaming competition held on a Sunday.
- This marks a significant achievement for the Chinese team in esports.


